NOTICE

This module patches defects in the Crucible game system and the Ember premium
module for Foundry Virtual Tabletop. It is an unofficial, third-party work and
is not affiliated with or endorsed by Foundry Gaming LLC or Mage Hand Press.

The MIT license above covers only the original code in this repository. It does
not grant any rights to Crucible or Ember themselves, neither of which is
redistributed here — this module contains no assets, compendium content, or
packaged code from either. Using it requires your own licensed installation.

Short excerpts of upstream source are quoted in the documentation. Two patches
reproduce upstream control flow for interoperability, because the defect they
fix sits mid-function and cannot be reached by wrapping: N1 (an Ember action
hook it must replace wholesale) and B4 (a Crucible method, reproduced with the
upstream fix applied). Both carry source-signature guards and retire themselves
once upstream changes the code they mirror. All such material remains the
property of its respective copyright holders.

Note that Crucible is distributed under a restrictive license which, at the
time of writing, grants no permission to modify, publish, or distribute the
system or its data. This module redistributes none of it — it patches at
runtime against the user's own licensed installation.
